# Project Governance (Mandatory)

TraderCity is in the Engineering Phase. Before implementing features or refactors, read:

1. `docs/00_Project_Governance/README.md`
2. `docs/00_Project_Governance/AI_DEVELOPMENT_GUIDELINES.md`
3. `docs/00_Project_Governance/PROJECT_ARCHITECTURE.md`
4. Domain docs under `docs/AI/Agents/<Domain>/` when relevant

## Standing rules

- Product Architecture ≠ Git Structure
- Git manages changes; it does not represent the product
- New work: `feature/*` from `develop` (or agreed integration baseline until `develop` exists)
- Investigations: `experiment/*` (temporary)
- Production emergencies: `hotfix/*`
- Never modify unrelated modules
- Never refactor without approval
- Never invent APIs or change backend contracts unless explicitly tasked
- Reuse existing design system and folder structure
- Preserve Marketing ↔ Admin isolation
- Do not bypass `TESTING_CHECKLIST.md` for UI merges
- Governance/docs tasks must not change application functionality
- Do not rename/delete long-lived branches unless explicitly tasked
